{"id":"fc4d04472af291f6","group":"17","path":"17/17-df-fraisse-class.md","title":"Fraïssé Classes, Ages, and Ultrahomogeneity","display":"df-fraisse-class — Fraïssé Classes, Ages, and Ultrahomogeneity","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Model Theory (Chang & Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)","book_abbrev":"17","label":"17-df-fraisse-class","aliases":["17-df-fraisse-class"],"display":"df-fraisse-class — Fraïssé Classes, Ages, and Ultrahomogeneity","depends_on":["[[17-df-embedding]]","[[17-df-first-order-language]]","[[17-df-structure]]","[[17-df-elementary-substructure]]","[[17-df-partial-isomorphism]]","[[17-df-isomorphism]]","[[17-df-set-functions]]","[[17-df-ordinals-finiteness]]","[[17-df-cardinal-arithmetic]]"],"label_origin":"local-catalog","source_verification":"not-compared-to-book-in-this-pass; local statement reviewed","local_revision":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Model Theory (Chang &amp; Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"17"},{"key":"label","html":"17-df-fraisse-class"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>17-df-fraisse-class</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-fraisse-class — Fraïssé Classes, Ages, and Ultrahomogeneity"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"3482e8f05d02c6f0\" href=\"?note=3482e8f05d02c6f0\" title=\"17-df-embedding\">17-df-embedding</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"dab75c9f48db057d\" href=\"?note=dab75c9f48db057d\" title=\"17-df-first-order-language\">17-df-first-order-language</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"fdac06af5a7f3bb5\" href=\"?note=fdac06af5a7f3bb5\" title=\"17-df-structure\">17-df-structure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"71ede582cb78a069\" href=\"?note=71ede582cb78a069\" title=\"17-df-elementary-substructure\">17-df-elementary-substructure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"f21d04ffa9b76787\" href=\"?note=f21d04ffa9b76787\" title=\"17-df-partial-isomorphism\">17-df-partial-isomorphism</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"9f3187e8ff79e64e\" href=\"?note=9f3187e8ff79e64e\" title=\"17-df-isomorphism\">17-df-isomorphism</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"571123944253d721\" href=\"?note=571123944253d721\" title=\"17-df-set-functions\">17-df-set-functions</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"b6e4a36b436c9b93\" href=\"?note=b6e4a36b436c9b93\" title=\"17-df-ordinals-finiteness\">17-df-ordinals-finiteness</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"0c4dd6e6f689f962\" href=\"?note=0c4dd6e6f689f962\" title=\"17-df-cardinal-arithmetic\">17-df-cardinal-arithmetic</a></span></div>"},{"key":"label_origin","html":"local-catalog"},{"key":"source_verification","html":"not-compared-to-book-in-this-pass; local statement reviewed"},{"key":"local_revision","html":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K\">\\(K\\)</span> 是以固定集合论公式给出的 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>-结构元类；涉及 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K\">\\(K\\)</span> 的量词是该公式的受限量词展开，而非 ZFC 中对真类的量化。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K_0\">\\(K_0\\)</span> 是一个集合，承担可数同构代表集的角色。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PartIso}\">\\(\\operatorname{PartIso}\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\cong_L\">\\(\\cong_L\\)</span> 的语言始终为此处固定的 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>，见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"f21d04ffa9b76787\" href=\"?note=f21d04ffa9b76787\" title=\"17-df-partial-isomorphism\">17-df-partial-isomorphism</a>、<a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-11\" data-note=\"9f3187e8ff79e64e\" href=\"?note=9f3187e8ff79e64e\" title=\"17-df-isomorphism\">17-df-isomorphism</a>。</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Emb}_L(f,\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak B)\">\\(\\operatorname{Emb}_L(f,\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak B)\\)</span> 为 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-12\" data-note=\"3482e8f05d02c6f0\" href=\"?note=3482e8f05d02c6f0\" title=\"17-df-embedding\">17-df-embedding</a> 的普通结构嵌入；与此前全定义域部分同构的接口等价。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\">\\(L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\\)</span> (first-order language, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-13\" data-note=\"dab75c9f48db057d\" href=\"?note=dab75c9f48db057d\" title=\"17-df-first-order-language\">17-df-first-order-language</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\">\\(\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\\)</span> (class of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>-structures, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-14\" data-note=\"fdac06af5a7f3bb5\" href=\"?note=fdac06af5a7f3bb5\" title=\"17-df-structure\">17-df-structure</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\subseteq_L\">\\(\\subseteq_L\\)</span> (substructure relation, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-15\" data-note=\"71ede582cb78a069\" href=\"?note=71ede582cb78a069\" title=\"17-df-elementary-substructure\">17-df-elementary-substructure</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PartIso}\">\\(\\operatorname{PartIso}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\cong\">\\(\\cong\\)</span> (partial isomorphism and isomorphism, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-16\" data-note=\"f21d04ffa9b76787\" href=\"?note=f21d04ffa9b76787\" title=\"17-df-partial-isomorphism\">17-df-partial-isomorphism</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-17\" data-note=\"9f3187e8ff79e64e\" href=\"?note=9f3187e8ff79e64e\" title=\"17-df-isomorphism\">17-df-isomorphism</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{dom}\">\\(\\operatorname{dom}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ran}\">\\(\\operatorname{ran}\\)</span> (domain and range, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-18\" data-note=\"571123944253d721\" href=\"?note=571123944253d721\" title=\"17-df-set-functions\">17-df-set-functions</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-19\" data-note=\"571123944253d721\" href=\"?note=571123944253d721\" title=\"17-df-set-functions\">17-df-set-functions</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\circ\">\\(\\circ\\)</span> (function composition, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-20\" data-note=\"571123944253d721\" href=\"?note=571123944253d721\" title=\"17-df-set-functions\">17-df-set-functions</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Finite}\">\\(\\operatorname{Finite}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|\\cdot|\">\\(|\\cdot|\\)</span> (finite-set and cardinality operators, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-21\" data-note=\"b6e4a36b436c9b93\" href=\"?note=b6e4a36b436c9b93\" title=\"17-df-ordinals-finiteness\">17-df-ordinals-finiteness</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-22\" data-note=\"0c4dd6e6f689f962\" href=\"?note=0c4dd6e6f689f962\" title=\"17-df-cardinal-arithmetic\">17-df-cardinal-arithmetic</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_0\">\\(\\aleph_0\\)</span> (least infinite cardinal, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-23\" data-note=\"0c4dd6e6f689f962\" href=\"?note=0c4dd6e6f689f962\" title=\"17-df-cardinal-arithmetic\">17-df-cardinal-arithmetic</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{FinStr}_L,\\operatorname{CountableIsoTypes}_L,\\operatorname{HP}_L,\\operatorname{JEP}_L,\\operatorname{AP}^{\\mathrm{fin}}_L,\\operatorname{FraisseClass}_L,\\operatorname{Age}_L,\\operatorname{LocallyFinite}_L,\\operatorname{Ultrahomogeneous}_L\">\\(\\operatorname{FinStr}_L,\\operatorname{CountableIsoTypes}_L,\\operatorname{HP}_L,\\operatorname{JEP}_L,\\operatorname{AP}^{\\mathrm{fin}}_L,\\operatorname{FraisseClass}_L,\\operatorname{Age}_L,\\operatorname{LocallyFinite}_L,\\operatorname{Ultrahomogeneous}_L\\)</span> (objects defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\quad\n\\operatorname{FinStr}_L\n&amp;\\coloneqq\n\\{\\mathfrak A\\in\\mathrm{Structure}(L):\n\\operatorname{Finite}(|\\mathfrak A|)\\},\\\\\n\\operatorname{CountableIsoTypes}_L(K)\n&amp;\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists K_0\\subseteq K\\;\n\\Bigl(\n|K_0|\\leq\\aleph_0\n\\land\n\\forall\\mathfrak A\\in K\\;\n\\exists\\mathfrak B\\in K_0\\;\n(\\mathfrak A\\cong\\mathfrak B)\n\\Bigr),\\\\\n\\operatorname{HP}_L(K)\n&amp;\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall\\mathfrak A\\in K\\;\\forall\\mathfrak B\\in\\operatorname{FinStr}_L\\;\n(\\mathfrak B\\subseteq_L\\mathfrak A\\to\\mathfrak B\\in K),\\\\\n\\operatorname{JEP}_L(K)\n&amp;\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak B\\in K\\;\n\\exists\\mathfrak C\\in K\\;\\exists f\\,\\exists g\\;\n\\bigl(\n\\operatorname{Emb}_L(f,\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak C)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{Emb}_L(g,\\mathfrak B,\\mathfrak C)\n\\bigr),\\\\\n\\operatorname{AP}^{\\mathrm{fin}}_L(K)\n&amp;\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak B,\\mathfrak C\\in K\\;\\forall f\\,\\forall g\n\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{Emb}_L(f,\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak B)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{Emb}_L(g,\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak C)\n\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{24mm}\\to\n\\exists\\mathfrak D\\in K\\;\\exists h\\,\\exists k\\;\n\\bigl(\n\\operatorname{Emb}_L(h,\\mathfrak B,\\mathfrak D)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{Emb}_L(k,\\mathfrak C,\\mathfrak D)\n\\land\nh\\circ f=k\\circ g\n\\bigr)\n\\Bigr),\\\\\n\\operatorname{FraisseClass}_L(K)\n&amp;\\leftrightarrow\nL\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\n\\land\n\\varnothing\\neq K\\subseteq\\operatorname{FinStr}_L\n\\\\\n&amp;\\quad{}\\land\n\\forall\\mathfrak A\\in K\\;\\forall\\mathfrak B\\in\\operatorname{FinStr}_L\\;\n(\\mathfrak A\\cong\\mathfrak B\\to\\mathfrak B\\in K)\n\\\\\n&amp;\\quad{}\\land\n\\operatorname{CountableIsoTypes}_L(K)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{HP}_L(K)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{JEP}_L(K)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{AP}^{\\mathrm{fin}}_L(K),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Age}_L(\\mathfrak M)\n&amp;\\coloneqq\n\\bigl\\{\n\\mathfrak A\\in\\operatorname{FinStr}_L:\n\\exists\\mathfrak B\\in\\operatorname{FinStr}_L\\;\n(\\mathfrak B\\subseteq_L\\mathfrak M\n\\land\n\\mathfrak A\\cong\\mathfrak B)\n\\bigr\\},\\\\\n\\operatorname{LocallyFinite}_L(\\mathfrak M)\n&amp;\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathfrak M\\in\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\n\\land\\forall X\\subseteq|\\mathfrak M|\\;\n\\Bigl(\\operatorname{Finite}(X)\\to\n\\exists\\mathfrak B\\in\\operatorname{FinStr}_L\\;\n(\\mathfrak B\\subseteq_L\\mathfrak M\\land X\\subseteq|\\mathfrak B|)\\Bigr),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Ultrahomogeneous}_L(\\mathfrak M)\n&amp;\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathfrak M\\in\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\n\\land\n\\forall\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak B\\in\\operatorname{FinStr}_L\\;\\forall p\n\\Bigl(\n\\mathfrak A\\subseteq_L\\mathfrak M\n\\land\n\\mathfrak B\\subseteq_L\\mathfrak M\n\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{14mm}\\land\n\\operatorname{PartIso}(p,\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak B)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{dom}(p)=|\\mathfrak A|\n\\land\n\\operatorname{ran}(p)=|\\mathfrak B|\n\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{14mm}\\to\n\\exists q\\;\n\\bigl(\n\\operatorname{PartIso}(q,\\mathfrak M,\\mathfrak M)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{dom}(q)=|\\mathfrak M|\n\\land\n\\operatorname{ran}(q)=|\\mathfrak M|\n\\land\np\\subseteq q\n\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\quad\n\\operatorname{FinStr}_L\n&amp;\\coloneqq\n\\{\\mathfrak A\\in\\mathrm{Structure}(L):\n\\operatorname{Finite}(|\\mathfrak A|)\\},\\\\\n\\operatorname{CountableIsoTypes}_L(K)\n&amp;\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists K_0\\subseteq K\\;\n\\Bigl(\n|K_0|\\leq\\aleph_0\n\\land\n\\forall\\mathfrak A\\in K\\;\n\\exists\\mathfrak B\\in K_0\\;\n(\\mathfrak A\\cong\\mathfrak B)\n\\Bigr),\\\\\n\\operatorname{HP}_L(K)\n&amp;\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall\\mathfrak A\\in K\\;\\forall\\mathfrak B\\in\\operatorname{FinStr}_L\\;\n(\\mathfrak B\\subseteq_L\\mathfrak A\\to\\mathfrak B\\in K),\\\\\n\\operatorname{JEP}_L(K)\n&amp;\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak B\\in K\\;\n\\exists\\mathfrak C\\in K\\;\\exists f\\,\\exists g\\;\n\\bigl(\n\\operatorname{Emb}_L(f,\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak C)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{Emb}_L(g,\\mathfrak B,\\mathfrak C)\n\\bigr),\\\\\n\\operatorname{AP}^{\\mathrm{fin}}_L(K)\n&amp;\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak B,\\mathfrak C\\in K\\;\\forall f\\,\\forall g\n\\Bigl(\n\\operatorname{Emb}_L(f,\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak B)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{Emb}_L(g,\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak C)\n\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{24mm}\\to\n\\exists\\mathfrak D\\in K\\;\\exists h\\,\\exists k\\;\n\\bigl(\n\\operatorname{Emb}_L(h,\\mathfrak B,\\mathfrak D)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{Emb}_L(k,\\mathfrak C,\\mathfrak D)\n\\land\nh\\circ f=k\\circ g\n\\bigr)\n\\Bigr),\\\\\n\\operatorname{FraisseClass}_L(K)\n&amp;\\leftrightarrow\nL\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\n\\land\n\\varnothing\\neq K\\subseteq\\operatorname{FinStr}_L\n\\\\\n&amp;\\quad{}\\land\n\\forall\\mathfrak A\\in K\\;\\forall\\mathfrak B\\in\\operatorname{FinStr}_L\\;\n(\\mathfrak A\\cong\\mathfrak B\\to\\mathfrak B\\in K)\n\\\\\n&amp;\\quad{}\\land\n\\operatorname{CountableIsoTypes}_L(K)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{HP}_L(K)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{JEP}_L(K)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{AP}^{\\mathrm{fin}}_L(K),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Age}_L(\\mathfrak M)\n&amp;\\coloneqq\n\\bigl\\{\n\\mathfrak A\\in\\operatorname{FinStr}_L:\n\\exists\\mathfrak B\\in\\operatorname{FinStr}_L\\;\n(\\mathfrak B\\subseteq_L\\mathfrak M\n\\land\n\\mathfrak A\\cong\\mathfrak B)\n\\bigr\\},\\\\\n\\operatorname{LocallyFinite}_L(\\mathfrak M)\n&amp;\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathfrak M\\in\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\n\\land\\forall X\\subseteq|\\mathfrak M|\\;\n\\Bigl(\\operatorname{Finite}(X)\\to\n\\exists\\mathfrak B\\in\\operatorname{FinStr}_L\\;\n(\\mathfrak B\\subseteq_L\\mathfrak M\\land X\\subseteq|\\mathfrak B|)\\Bigr),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Ultrahomogeneous}_L(\\mathfrak M)\n&amp;\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathfrak M\\in\\mathrm{Structure}(L)\n\\land\n\\forall\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak B\\in\\operatorname{FinStr}_L\\;\\forall p\n\\Bigl(\n\\mathfrak A\\subseteq_L\\mathfrak M\n\\land\n\\mathfrak B\\subseteq_L\\mathfrak M\n\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{14mm}\\land\n\\operatorname{PartIso}(p,\\mathfrak A,\\mathfrak B)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{dom}(p)=|\\mathfrak A|\n\\land\n\\operatorname{ran}(p)=|\\mathfrak B|\n\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{14mm}\\to\n\\exists q\\;\n\\bigl(\n\\operatorname{PartIso}(q,\\mathfrak M,\\mathfrak M)\n\\land\n\\operatorname{dom}(q)=|\\mathfrak M|\n\\land\n\\operatorname{ran}(q)=|\\mathfrak M|\n\\land\np\\subseteq q\n\\bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Emb}_L\">\\(\\operatorname{Emb}_L\\)</span> is imported from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-24\" data-note=\"3482e8f05d02c6f0\" href=\"?note=3482e8f05d02c6f0\" title=\"17-df-embedding\">17-df-embedding</a>; its component definition is equivalent to the previous total-partial-isomorphism clause. It preserves the same argument order and ordinary-embedding meaning.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{CountableIsoTypes}_L\">\\(\\operatorname{CountableIsoTypes}_L\\)</span> uses a countable representative subcollection rather than a quotient by a potentially proper-class isomorphism relation.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Ultrahomogeneous}_L\">\\(\\operatorname{Ultrahomogeneous}_L\\)</span> says every isomorphism between finite substructures extends to an automorphism of the whole structure.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The local finiteness predicate ensures that every finite set of elements lies in a finite substructure. This is necessary for finite-age uniqueness in function languages. These Fraïssé notions are supplementary local material: a matching Fraïssé-limit statement has not been located in the supplied book by full OCR term searches. No original book numbering or source verification is claimed.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"17-df-embedding","status":"resolved","id":"3482e8f05d02c6f0","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-embedding]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-first-order-language","status":"resolved","id":"dab75c9f48db057d","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-first-order-language]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-structure","status":"resolved","id":"fdac06af5a7f3bb5","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-structure]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-elementary-substructure","status":"resolved","id":"71ede582cb78a069","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-elementary-substructure]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-partial-isomorphism","status":"resolved","id":"f21d04ffa9b76787","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-partial-isomorphism]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-isomorphism","status":"resolved","id":"9f3187e8ff79e64e","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-isomorphism]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-set-functions","status":"resolved","id":"571123944253d721","anchor":